#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""jamai-hub — the service beside your melody page: people subscribe, and each new melody reaches them.

  jamai-hub serve [--host H] [--port P]   the melody page, the subscription routes, the delivery worker
  jamai-hub invite [LABEL]                a one-use invite code to hand to a person
  jamai-hub subscriptions                 who is subscribed (never the secrets)
  jamai-hub events [N]                    the last N facts in the ledger
  jamai-hub deliveries [N]                the last N delivery attempts
  jamai-hub unit                          a systemd user unit, to keep the hub running

How it fits together
  jamai-publish-melody appends one fact per new or revised melody to the ledger
  ($JAMAI_STATE_DIR/events/ledger.jsonl) and delivers nothing itself. The hub reads the ledger and
  POSTs each fact once to every subscription that asked for its type, signed with the
  subscription's own secret:  X-JamAI-Signature: sha256=<HMAC-SHA256 of the body>.

Routes (all relative, so the hub works behind any path prefix)
  GET  /                              the subscribe page
  GET  /melody/…                      your melody folder, read-only
  GET  /api/events[?after=ID&limit=N] the facts, oldest first
  GET  /api/melodies                  the published melodies, without their ABC source
  POST /api/subscriptions             {"url", "events"?, "label"?, "invite"?}  →  {"id", "secret"}
  GET  /api/subscriptions/ID          Authorization: Bearer <secret>
  POST /api/subscriptions/ID/ping     send a test delivery now
  DELETE /api/subscriptions/ID        end the subscription
  GET  /api/admin/subscriptions       Authorization: Bearer <JAMAI_HUB_ADMIN_TOKEN>
  POST /api/admin/invites             {"label"?}  →  {"code"}

Safety, on by default
  A webhook must be https and must resolve to a public address, checked again at each delivery
  and pinned for the connection (JAMAI_HUB_ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS=1 lifts this, for tests).
  Redirects are not followed. Subscribing needs an invite code unless JAMAI_HUB_OPEN_SUBSCRIPTIONS=1.

Python standard library only.
"""
